# declared skips for the spirv column. one entry per line:
#   <case-glob>  <layers>[:<profiles>]  <reason>
# layers is any of a, b, c, or * for all three. naming pipelines after a colon
# declares away those cells and no others, so a defect that is one pipeline wide
# leaves the pipelines either side of it reporting. a skip counts as a skip in the
# matrix, never as a pass, and the run fails on an empty cell that has no entry here.
#
# layer c needs no entry: engines.conf declares engine none for this target, which
# the matrix reports as its own label.
#
# entries are written out by name rather than globbed by family, so a case added
# later inherits nothing and has to be reviewed against this file on its way in.
#
# two kinds of entry live here and they are not interchangeable.
#
#   TARGET LIMITATION. SPIR-V cannot express the construct. the corpus has no
#   question to ask, and the entry stays until the target or the language changes.
#
#   MACH DEFECT. SPIR-V can express the construct and mach does not emit it, either
#   refusing to build or writing a module spirv-val rejects. the corpus has a
#   question and mach cannot yet answer it. every one of these names an issue and is
#   deleted by the change that closes it, not by anyone tidying this file.
#
# a layer B entry accompanies every layer A entry, including the cases that build
# and fail only validation. blessing a golden from a module the validator rejects
# would record broken output as the code we meant to generate, which is worse than
# having no golden at all.
#
# 58 of the 90 cases build and validate for spirv and carry the column. the 32 below
# do not.

# ---- TARGET LIMITATION ----

call/call_recursive  ab  a SPIR-V execution model has no call stack, so a function may not be reachable from itself: "this call graph is a cycle and the SPIR-V target cannot express it: descend -> descend". recursion at four shapes is what the case is, so there is nothing to narrow.
call/call_chain      ab  same refusal, "chain -> chain". the case holds values live across a self-recursive chain by construction.
cmp/short_circuit    ab  "a plain module-scope variable is not reachable from the SPIR-V target: a shader has no general global storage, so a module-scope `val` / `var` reaches a stage only by carrying an interface role". the case proves non-evaluation through side-effect counters, which have to be module-scope state.
mem/global_data      ab  same refusal. module-scope initialized storage is the case.
mem/global_zero      ab  same refusal. module-scope zero-initialized storage is the case.
mem/uni_layout       ab  a uni has no SPIR-V type: passed by value it is "unsupported parameter type in the SPIR-V target", and held locally it is "unsupported local allocation type in the SPIR-V target". a raw union read back through a second member is the case.

# ---- MACH DEFECT ----

scalar/arith_u8    ab  #2919 an 8- or 16-bit loop counter is allocated 64-bit while its bound keeps the declared width, so spirv-val rejects the module mach reported success for: "Expected both operands to have the same component bit width: ULessThan". a u32 counter is clean, so this is the counter width alone.
scalar/arith_u16   ab  #2919 same, ULessThan on a 16-bit bound against a 64-bit counter.
scalar/arith_i8    ab  #2919 same, SLessThan.
scalar/arith_i16   ab  #2919 same, SLessThan.
cmp/cmp_u32        ab  #2910 a comparison result reaches spirv as %bool and is passed where the callee declares %uchar, with no OpSelect between: "OpFunctionCall Argument's type does not match Function's parameter type". every predicate in the case folds through mix_u8 by contract.
cmp/cmp_u64        ab  #2910 same.
cmp/cmp_i32        ab  #2910 same.
cmp/cmp_i64        ab  #2910 same.
float/cmp_f32      ab  #2910 same, on float predicates.
float/cmp_f64      ab  #2910 same.
float/special_f32  ab  #2910 same. the case folds an is-NaN predicate, which is a comparison result crossing a call.
float/special_f64  ab  #2910 same.
call/call_rec_small  ab  #2914 a record passed by value reaches the back end as addressed memory: "addressed memory is not yet supported by the SPIR-V target ... (MIR_STORE in fold_r1)". logical addressing expresses an OpTypeStruct parameter directly, so this is a missing lowering rather than a target bound.
call/call_rec_edge   ab  #2914 same, in fold_e9.
call/call_rec_large  ab  #2914 same, in fold_l24.
call/call_ret_large  ab  #2914 same, in fold20.
call/call_indirect   ab  #2914 same, in fold24.
mem/loadstore        ab  #2914 same, in fold_packed. the case itself uses only local records, arrays and a pointer to a scalar, all of which the target accepts.
mem/rec_layout       ab  #2914 same, in fold_tiny, plus fill_mid's *Mid parameter refused as "unsupported parameter type in the SPIR-V target".
mem/array_index      ab  #2914 same, in fold_cell.
mem/ptr_arith        ab  #2914 same, in fold_cell. an interior pointer on its own builds and validates, so the record-valued fold helper is what blocks the case and this entry goes when #2914 does.
call/call_ret_small  ab  #2915 a record returned by value refuses with a bare internal message and no location, "spirv.emit: unreadable move source", while the same limitation in the argument direction gets a full explanatory refusal.
call/call_mixed      ab  #2923 "more than 16 parameters is not supported by the SPIR-V target (in mixed)". SPIR-V allows 255 and types.mach says the sixteen is the emitter's own fixed operand buffer. the case exists to exhaust the integer and float banks in one signature, which needs eighteen, so it cannot be shortened without giving up what it tests.
vec/vec_cmp_select   ab  #2920 a 16-byte vector bit reinterpret declares a scalar OpTypeInt 128 alongside the correct OpBitcast, and spirv-val refuses the module mach reported success for: "Invalid number of bits (128) used for OpTypeInt". the same reinterpret is correct on x86_64 and riscv64, where the case passes layer C.
vec/vec_mem          ab  #2922 whole-record assignment lowers to an address into local storage: "a function-local object is reachable from the SPIR-V target only as a whole value ... it is a lowering that ran where it should not have". reproduces on a scalar-only record, so it is not vector-related.
vec/autovec_loop     ab:o2  #2921 three sequential array loops are refused only at -O2, "a loop whose exits do not reconverge on one block is not yet supported by the SPIR-V target", because the pipeline restructures them into a shape the emitter will not take. o0 and g build and validate and are deliberately left reporting: they are the evidence that this is the optimizer and not the source.
